    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11952" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπέριττος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without superfluity, plain,
				simple,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιτοὶ καὶ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Zeno Stoic.
					1.57
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.267f
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VS</u>
				1.23.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀ. τῆς τροφῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Nigr.</u>
					26
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηροί, γαστήρ,</span>
			<i>perfectly modelled,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
			</span></i> Jun.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Im.</u>
				14
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				15
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ττως</span>”
				<i>plainly,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					12.26
				</span></i>
			; <i>frugally,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Simp.
				<u>in Epict.</u>
				p.33
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i></div>
